- What are you doing here?

263
00:14:32,914 --> 00:14:33,915
Well...

264
00:14:36,584 --> 00:14:39,629
it occurred to me that I've never
snuck through your bedroom window.

265
00:14:40,380 --> 00:14:42,548
I was home, bored,

266
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:44,967
watching TV...

267
00:14:45,051 --> 00:14:46,052
Mmm.

268
00:14:49,430 --> 00:14:51,057
...and <i>Stab</i> was on.

269
00:14:52,016 --> 00:14:53,851
And that just got me thinking of you.

270
00:14:53,935 --> 00:14:55,520
That's horrific.

271
00:14:55,603 --> 00:14:57,397
Billy snuck through Sidney's window, so...

272
00:14:57,480 --> 00:15:00,024
Mm-hmm. I'm well aware.

273
00:15:00,108 --> 00:15:02,235
You know, if my mom catches you...

274
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:04,695
Mmm. Just a kiss.

275
00:15:14,831 --> 00:15:15,832
Hey.

276
00:15:15,915 --> 00:15:17,041
Hi.

277
00:15:23,506 --> 00:15:24,549
- [knocking on door]
- [boyfriend] Oh!

278
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:26,134
[body thuds]

279
00:15:26,217 --> 00:15:27,427
[door opens]

280
00:15:28,177 --> 00:15:29,679
Can you knock?

281
00:15:29,762 --> 00:15:31,305
I did.

282
00:15:31,389 --> 00:15:32,598
Can you wait for a response?

283
00:15:33,307 --> 00:15:34,308
Something wrong?

284
00:15:34,892 --> 00:15:36,227
No.

285
00:15:36,310 --> 00:15:37,854
- No, everything's fine.
- You sure?

286
00:15:37,937 --> 00:15:38,813
Mm-hmm.

287
00:15:39,564 --> 00:15:41,566
Ben, how you doing over there?

288
00:15:41,649 --> 00:15:44,193
On the floor. Behind the bed.

289
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:47,738
Hello, Mrs. Evans.

290
00:15:47,822 --> 00:15:49,282
How are you this evening?

291
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:52,326
Oh, well, I'm tired. Ben, it's late.

292
00:15:52,410 --> 00:15:55,580
That's why I didn't want to
disturb anyone by...

293
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:57,039
using the door.

294
00:15:57,123 --> 00:15:58,583
So thoughtful.

295
00:15:59,709 --> 00:16:00,585
Out.

296
00:16:00,668 --> 00:16:02,336
- But he's here now.
- No.

297
00:16:02,420 --> 00:16:04,088
That's okay. I'm going.

298
00:16:08,885 --> 00:16:10,511
Good night, Tate.

299
00:16:15,725 --> 00:16:18,769
[Ben] I know it's late.
I'm sorry, Mrs. Evans.

300
00:16:18,853 --> 00:16:21,856
That was on me.
Tatum had no idea that I was coming over.

301
00:16:21,939 --> 00:16:24,942
Okay, well, let's not do it again.

302
00:16:27,570 --> 00:16:28,613
[sighs]

303
00:16:32,200 --> 00:16:33,701
I'm a good guy, Mrs. Evans.

304
00:16:33,784 --> 00:16:35,036
Good night, Ben.

305
00:16:46,088 --> 00:16:47,381
Hypocrite.

306
00:16:50,301 --> 00:16:51,636
[scoffs]

307
00:16:55,097 --> 00:16:57,808
It's not like a boy's never
crawled through your window.

308
00:16:57,892 --> 00:16:59,894
- [phone chimes]
- We've all seen the movie.

309
00:16:59,977 --> 00:17:02,438
Which is why it's never
gonna happen in this house.

310
00:17:03,189 --> 00:17:04,315
Why do you not like him?

311
00:17:05,233 --> 00:17:06,526
[sighs]

312
00:17:06,609 --> 00:17:07,902
I don't not like him.

313
00:17:07,985 --> 00:17:09,779
I just-- I want you to be smart.

314
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:11,781
And not trust him so easily.

315
00:17:11,864 --> 00:17:12,907
We're not having sex,

316
00:17:12,990 --> 00:17:14,867
if that's what you're worried about.

317
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:16,994
I mean, we want to,

318
00:17:18,579 --> 00:17:20,122
but I don't think we're ready.

319
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:23,125
Well, if you're asking
the question, then, um...

320
00:17:23,876 --> 00:17:25,545
you're probably not.

321
00:17:25,628 --> 00:17:26,963
How did you know?

322
00:17:30,716 --> 00:17:32,760
I mean, did that really happen to you?

323
00:17:33,386 --> 00:17:34,387
Like in the movie?

324
00:17:37,473 --> 00:17:39,225
It's freezing in here.

325
00:17:40,309 --> 00:17:41,561
[Sidney exhales]

326
00:17:45,815 --> 00:17:47,400
How about we have
these kinds of conversations

327
00:17:47,483 --> 00:17:49,485
during waking hours, okay?

328
00:17:49,569 --> 00:17:52,738
No more boys in windows, please.

329
00:17:53,781 --> 00:17:54,782
[Sidney sighs]

330
00:17:56,576 --> 00:17:57,660
Night.

331
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:01,664
[sighs]

332
00:18:07,753 --> 00:18:09,005
How ugly did it get?

333
00:18:10,923 --> 00:18:12,550
I was extremely polite.

334
00:18:12,633 --> 00:18:14,468
You know, she's not the first girl

335
00:18:14,552 --> 00:18:16,095
to let a boy sneak in her window.

336
00:18:16,178 --> 00:18:18,472
Yeah. She made that point.

337
00:18:18,556 --> 00:18:20,349
You know, if being an overprotective mom

338
00:18:20,433 --> 00:18:22,560
is the worst thing she can
say about me... [sighs]

339
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:24,353
...I think I can live with that.

340
00:18:24,437 --> 00:18:25,730
You think they're doing it?

341
00:18:25,813 --> 00:18:28,232
Oh, God, no.

342
00:18:28,316 --> 00:18:31,027
[chuckles] No. Not yet.

343
00:18:31,110 --> 00:18:33,237
But I think we've got
about five minutes left.

344
00:18:34,780 --> 00:18:36,866
How old were you when you started?

345
00:18:36,949 --> 00:18:39,035
Same age as you. Seventeen.

346
00:18:39,118 --> 00:18:41,996
Oh, did I say seventeen?
I think I meant fifteen.

347
00:18:43,748 --> 00:18:44,874
Did you lie to me?

348
00:18:44,957 --> 00:18:48,044
Look, in my defense, I don't remember.

349
00:18:48,127 --> 00:18:50,379
Oh, you don't remember
the first time you had sex?

350
00:18:50,463 --> 00:18:52,423
Oh, no, I don't remember what I told you.

351
00:18:52,506 --> 00:18:54,675
Oh, you told me seventeen.

352
00:18:54,759 --> 00:18:57,720
Look, I didn't want to
come off as, you know...

353
00:18:57,803 --> 00:18:59,639
Uh-huh. Keep going.
I want to see where this goes.

354
00:18:59,722 --> 00:19:01,807
[stammers] I just wanted you to see me

355
00:19:01,891 --> 00:19:03,684
as more than a sex slave.

356
00:19:03,768 --> 00:19:06,854
Oh. You have a mind, too?

357
00:19:06,937 --> 00:19:08,981
You know... well, yeah.

358
00:19:09,065 --> 00:19:11,067
[gentle music playing]

359
00:19:20,034 --> 00:19:22,161
[people chuckling]

360
00:19:22,244 --> 00:19:24,580
[rock music playing]

361
00:19:24,664 --> 00:19:26,749
[saw whirring]

362
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:28,042
[people chattering indistinctly]

363
00:19:30,252 --> 00:19:31,504
[contractor] Morning, Chief.

364
00:19:31,587 --> 00:19:33,297
Hey, Woody. Look at that,
the walls are up, right?

365
00:19:33,381 --> 00:19:34,965
Looks great.

366
00:19:35,049 --> 00:19:37,385
- [child on tablet] <i>Love you.</i>
- I love you, too. We miss you guys.

367
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:39,387
- [Mark] Construction's coming along.
<i>- We're keeping them busy.</i>

368
00:19:39,470 --> 00:19:41,347
- Oh. Hey, Mom.
- [mother] <i>Hi there, baby.</i>

369
00:19:41,430 --> 00:19:43,307
- [child] <i>Hi, Daddy.</i>
- Thanks, Junie.

370
00:19:43,391 --> 00:19:44,600
I'm glad you're having fun.

371
00:19:44,684 --> 00:19:46,435
- If you need anything, call.
<i>- Okay.</i>

372
00:19:46,519 --> 00:19:48,771
I love you. Thank you
for watching the maniacs.

373
00:19:48,854 --> 00:19:50,314
We'll see you this weekend.

374
00:19:50,398 --> 00:19:51,273
<i>- Bye.</i>
- Bye.

375
00:19:51,357 --> 00:19:52,191
[tablet chimes]

376
00:19:52,274 --> 00:19:54,527
- She's very brave.
- Yep.

377
00:19:57,697 --> 00:19:59,782
- [ominous music plays]
- [saw whirs]

378
00:20:01,659 --> 00:20:02,660
What?

379
00:20:03,661 --> 00:20:05,329
Where'd you find that?

380
00:20:05,413 --> 00:20:06,914
Um, the attic.

381
00:20:06,997 --> 00:20:08,499
I was looking through some old clothes.

382
00:20:11,669 --> 00:20:13,337
Do you not want me to wear it?

383
00:20:13,421 --> 00:20:14,714
You could have asked.

384
00:20:17,508 --> 00:20:19,051
Honey, maybe take it off.

385
00:20:25,850 --> 00:20:27,727
What age do they get nice again?

386
00:20:29,562 --> 00:20:30,896
That was on you.

387
00:20:32,898 --> 00:20:34,233
[inhales deeply]

388
00:20:34,859 --> 00:20:36,736
[sighs]

389
00:20:39,572 --> 00:20:41,073
[mysterious music plays]

390
00:20:42,199 --> 00:20:43,451
[sighs]

391
00:20:46,787 --> 00:20:48,539
You can wear the jacket.

392
00:20:49,415 --> 00:20:50,583
It's okay, I'm good.

393
00:20:51,167 --> 00:20:53,002
Tatum, I'm sorry.

394
00:20:53,085 --> 00:20:54,503
Okay? It caught me off guard.

395
00:20:54,587 --> 00:20:56,046
I hadn't seen it since college.

396
00:20:56,130 --> 00:20:58,174
I thought I'd gotten rid of it.

397
00:20:58,257 --> 00:21:00,968
Yeah, the mysterious one semester
at Windsor we can't talk about.

398
00:21:01,051 --> 00:21:02,178
That's not true.

399
00:21:02,261 --> 00:21:04,680
Really? Since when?

400
00:21:04,764 --> 00:21:07,266
Your childhood is completely off-limits.

401
00:21:07,349 --> 00:21:10,269
[laughs] What are you talking about?
It's not off-limits.

402
00:21:10,352 --> 00:21:12,188
It's online and in movies and in books.

403
00:21:12,271 --> 00:21:14,064
You could do a deep dive
whenever you want.

404
00:21:14,148 --> 00:21:15,775
As long as I don't ask questions.

405
00:21:19,612 --> 00:21:21,447
You have rehearsal today?

406
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:23,949
Yep.

407
00:21:25,618 --> 00:21:26,952
How's it going?

408
00:21:29,663 --> 00:21:30,664
Horrible.

409
00:21:31,373 --> 00:21:33,459
Tragic. [chuckles]

410
00:21:33,542 --> 00:21:36,128
I get so nervous onstage,
it's painful to watch.

411
00:21:36,212 --> 00:21:39,548
Oh, God! I used to get stage fright.
I know the feeling.

412
00:21:40,299 --> 00:21:42,051
You did theater?

413
00:21:44,094 --> 00:21:45,429
Not since college.

414
00:21:47,515 --> 00:21:50,851
Anyway, don't worry.
You're gonna do great.

415
00:21:52,812 --> 00:21:54,313
I got to get to work.

416
00:21:59,443 --> 00:22:01,070
Fucking motherhood.

417
00:22:01,153 --> 00:22:02,905
Great talk.

418
00:22:02,988 --> 00:22:04,990
["The Kill" playing]

419
00:22:30,224 --> 00:22:33,227
["The Kill" continues through speakers]

420
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:36,814
- Morning.
- Hey, morning.

421
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,280
[server] We'll have that
right out for you. Okay?

422
00:22:44,363 --> 00:22:45,865
[customer] All right. Thank you.

423
00:22:45,948 --> 00:22:48,075
- Busy?
- Little AM rush, but not too bad.

424
00:22:48,158 --> 00:22:49,285
Good. [sighs]

425
00:22:49,368 --> 00:22:51,787
- Hey, Mrs. Evans.
- Hey, Lucas.

426
00:22:51,871 --> 00:22:53,873
Oh, could I get
four espresso shots, please?

427
00:22:53,956 --> 00:22:54,957
Yeah. For sure.

428
00:22:55,040 --> 00:22:57,418
- Four?
- Yeah. [chuckles]

429
00:22:57,501 --> 00:22:59,753
Rehearsal today. It's gonna be a long one.

430
00:22:59,837 --> 00:23:01,338
What part do you play?

431
00:23:01,422 --> 00:23:02,548
Oh, just a techie. Yeah.

432
00:23:02,631 --> 00:23:05,217
I work the, uh-- the lighting board.

433
00:23:05,301 --> 00:23:07,303
- Cool.
- Yeah. [inhales sharply]

434
00:23:07,386 --> 00:23:08,804
Hey, an old <i>Dateline</i> was on last night

435
00:23:08,888 --> 00:23:10,180
about the Ghostface Killers in New York.

436
00:23:10,264 --> 00:23:11,557
Have you, uh-- Have you seen it?

437
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:13,976
No, I haven't.

438
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:16,520
It's not as good as the Netflix doc,
but it's decent.

439
00:23:16,604 --> 00:23:18,480
They did a good job
covering the aftermath.

440
00:23:18,564 --> 00:23:20,190
[sighs] Morning.

441
00:23:20,274 --> 00:23:21,483
Hey.

442
00:23:21,567 --> 00:23:22,818
- Did you say anything?
- Mm-mmm.

443
00:23:22,902 --> 00:23:24,111
Did he ask you about <i>Dateline</i>?

444
00:23:24,194 --> 00:23:25,404
It's fine, really.

445
00:23:25,487 --> 00:23:26,947
No, it isn't.

446
00:23:27,031 --> 00:23:28,240
- I told you not to.
- Ow!

447
00:23:28,324 --> 00:23:29,909
- That hurt.
- Good.

448
00:23:29,992 --> 00:23:33,370
I'm a crime junkie, Mom.
It's my-- It's my thing.

449
00:23:33,454 --> 00:23:35,831
[sighs] I'm sorry, Mrs. Evans.

450
00:23:35,915 --> 00:23:38,000
But I really want to start a podcast,

451
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:40,544
and I think the New York murders
would be a primo first case.

452
00:23:40,628 --> 00:23:42,880
Don't you have rehearsal now, honey?

453
00:23:42,963 --> 00:23:44,256
- Right?
- Yes.

454
00:23:44,340 --> 00:23:46,592
- So you should leave now.
- Right. Yeah. Okay.

455
00:23:46,675 --> 00:23:48,052
- Okay. Great.
- Bye.

456
00:23:48,135 --> 00:23:49,178
- Bye.
- Bye!

457
00:23:49,261 --> 00:23:52,056
- [sighs] I'm sorry.
- It's fine.

458
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:54,099
What'll you have?

459
00:23:54,183 --> 00:23:56,185
["The Kill" continues]

460
00:23:59,939 --> 00:24:01,774
["The Kill" continues through earbuds]

461
00:24:01,857 --> 00:24:03,734
[Tatum] Hey, wait up!

462
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:05,194
- [friend] Oh, hey.
- [friend 2] Hi!

463
00:24:05,277 --> 00:24:07,529
- You look hot.
- Where'd you get the jacket?

464
00:24:07,613 --> 00:24:09,782
Thanks. It's my mom's. '90s vintage.

465
00:24:09,865 --> 00:24:11,116
[gasps] You should bedazzle it.

466
00:24:11,200 --> 00:24:12,201
Yes.

467
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:14,244
Oh! Tonight, my place, party.

468
00:24:14,328 --> 00:24:15,871
I've been stockpiling my mom's edibles.

469
00:24:15,955 --> 00:24:17,957
And you can even invite creepy boy.

470
00:24:18,040 --> 00:24:19,625
Listen, he's not creepy.

471
00:24:19,708 --> 00:24:21,126
- Mmm.
- He's deep.

472
00:24:21,210 --> 00:24:23,003
- And he has a squeezy butt.
- Ew.

473
00:24:23,087 --> 00:24:25,881
The true crime is cringy.
He's obsessed with my mom.

474
00:24:25,965 --> 00:24:28,175
Is your mom gonna let you out
of your cage tonight?

475
00:24:28,258 --> 00:24:30,219
I-- [sighs] I don't know.

476
00:24:30,302 --> 00:24:33,722
Honestly, she's been on overdrive
with the mama trauma.

477
00:24:33,806 --> 00:24:37,059
Well, if anyone has a right
to be insane, it is your mom.

478
00:24:37,142 --> 00:24:38,936
Very true. I've seen all the <i>Stab</i> movies.

479
00:24:39,019 --> 00:24:41,271
Personally, I don't know how
she's not in a psych ward.

480
00:24:41,355 --> 00:24:42,356
[horn honks]

481
00:24:42,439 --> 00:24:43,440
- Oh.
- Oh.

482
00:24:43,524 --> 00:24:45,484
- Look who it is.
- [Ben] Hey!

483
00:24:45,567 --> 00:24:49,071
- Top of the morning!
- Hey, Tay.

484
00:24:49,154 --> 00:24:50,197
- Hey, babe.
- Hiya.

485
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:51,991
You all need a lift?

486
00:24:52,074 --> 00:24:53,742
- You guys, come on!
- Yes!

487
00:24:53,826 --> 00:24:57,079
- We don't have to walk anymore. Let's go!
- Yeah, yeah, yeah. Buckle up.

488
00:24:57,162 --> 00:24:58,914
[pop punk music playing]

489
00:24:58,998 --> 00:25:00,791
Buckle up. Buckle up!

490
00:25:01,750 --> 00:25:03,210
[teenagers laugh]

491
00:25:03,752 --> 00:25:04,670
Karl!

492
00:25:14,179 --> 00:25:15,764
Thank you.

493
00:25:16,682 --> 00:25:19,184
- I am so sorry about Lucas.
- No.

494
00:25:19,268 --> 00:25:21,437
It's just you're like a celebrity to him.

495
00:25:23,689 --> 00:25:25,607
You feel like you guys are close, right?

496
00:25:25,691 --> 00:25:29,987
Yeah. I mean, I suppose we've
had to be since it's just the two of us.

497
00:25:30,070 --> 00:25:33,866
Do you ever talk to him about
your life before you had him?

498
00:25:33,949 --> 00:25:35,200
- No.
- No?

499
00:25:35,284 --> 00:25:37,411
No, no. I mean, there's not much I can say

500
00:25:37,494 --> 00:25:39,371
about his abusive asshole father

501
00:25:39,455 --> 00:25:42,374
and how badly our marriage fucked me up.

502
00:25:42,458 --> 00:25:44,293
Why? What's going on?

503
00:25:44,376 --> 00:25:46,545
Oh, I don't know. Uh...

504
00:25:46,628 --> 00:25:49,298
Tatum and I are having
a bit of a rough patch.

505
00:25:49,381 --> 00:25:52,384
She's at that age where
she wants to know about my past.

506
00:25:52,468 --> 00:25:54,511
And as you know,
my past is full of dead people.

507
00:25:54,595 --> 00:25:57,556
Not exactly something
I want to share with her.

508
00:25:57,639 --> 00:26:00,434
So I get quiet, and then she gets loud,

509
00:26:00,517 --> 00:26:02,352
and around and around we go.

510
00:26:02,436 --> 00:26:04,354
Listen. She's your daughter,

511
00:26:04,438 --> 00:26:06,815
and it's natural
she should want to know you.

512
00:26:06,899 --> 00:26:08,484
You know, I just--
I want my kids to be able

513
00:26:08,567 --> 00:26:11,070
to be who they are without living in fear.

514
00:26:11,153 --> 00:26:13,655
I want them to feel safe and protected.

515
00:26:13,739 --> 00:26:15,657
But it's not a safe world, Sid.

516
00:26:15,741 --> 00:26:17,576
And if we protect our children too much,

517
00:26:17,659 --> 00:26:19,912
they'll never learn
how to protect themselves.

518
00:26:22,915 --> 00:26:26,085
