774
00:38:51,746 --> 00:38:53,164
[Sidney] Tatum, we're going.

775
00:38:54,541 --> 00:38:55,542
Not you.

776
00:38:56,709 --> 00:38:58,294
- Mom.
- Answer's no.

777
00:38:58,378 --> 00:38:59,462
But, Mrs. Evans--

778
00:38:59,546 --> 00:39:00,547
No.

779
00:39:04,008 --> 00:39:05,885
It's okay. You go with your family.

780
00:39:07,303 --> 00:39:08,471
I'll call you.

781
00:39:16,396 --> 00:39:17,939
Why do you treat him like that?

782
00:39:19,023 --> 00:39:20,024
He's not a killer.

783
00:39:20,108 --> 00:39:21,150
You don't know that.

784
00:39:21,234 --> 00:39:24,445
Not everyone is Billy Loomis.

785
00:39:24,529 --> 00:39:25,989
Just because you can't trust people,

786
00:39:26,072 --> 00:39:27,907
doesn't mean people can't be trusted.

787
00:39:28,867 --> 00:39:29,993
We're not doing this here.

788
00:39:34,289 --> 00:39:36,165
[suspenseful music playing]

789
00:39:45,049 --> 00:39:47,343
- They'll sweep the house.
- Yeah. We'll be quick, Chief.

790
00:40:08,865 --> 00:40:09,866
[deputy] All clear.

791
00:40:10,867 --> 00:40:12,201
We're gonna secure the neighborhood.

792
00:40:12,285 --> 00:40:13,494
Great. We'll only be a few minutes.

793
00:40:13,578 --> 00:40:14,579
- Come on.
- Thank you.

794
00:40:18,625 --> 00:40:20,543
Grab your stuff. You leave in five.

795
00:40:21,628 --> 00:40:24,213
Wait. You're not coming with us?

796
00:40:24,297 --> 00:40:26,382
It's my job to catch whoever's doing this.

797
00:40:37,769 --> 00:40:40,772
[ominous music plays]

798
00:40:40,855 --> 00:40:42,440
[music stops]

799
00:40:42,523 --> 00:40:43,566
Where's your go bag?

800
00:40:43,650 --> 00:40:45,735
I unpacked it a long time ago.

801
00:40:45,818 --> 00:40:47,070
Damn it, Tatum.

802
00:40:49,197 --> 00:40:50,281
[sighs]

803
00:40:52,200 --> 00:40:53,660
So, what? We just run?

804
00:40:53,743 --> 00:40:55,119
[sighs]

805
00:40:55,203 --> 00:40:56,663
Yes, we do.

806
00:40:56,746 --> 00:40:59,248
I thought the great
Sidney Prescott never ran.

807
00:40:59,332 --> 00:41:00,750
With you it's different.

808
00:41:01,501 --> 00:41:02,961
They killed Hannah, Mom.

809
00:41:03,044 --> 00:41:05,755
- We can't just leave.
- Listen, I know this story,

810
00:41:05,838 --> 00:41:08,341
and if we stay, more people will die.

811
00:41:08,424 --> 00:41:11,386
I'm sorry, but I'm not gonna
risk you getting hurt.

812
00:41:13,346 --> 00:41:14,472
Why didn't you warn me?

813
00:41:14,555 --> 00:41:16,516
- About what?
- All of this!

814
00:41:16,599 --> 00:41:19,352
If-If I was ready,
maybe I could have saved her.

815
00:41:19,435 --> 00:41:20,895
Maybe I could have done something.

816
00:41:20,979 --> 00:41:22,438
If you need anything else, pack it.

817
00:41:22,522 --> 00:41:24,399
Mom, why can't you just trust me?

818
00:41:24,482 --> 00:41:26,734
We need to go! Okay?

819
00:41:32,615 --> 00:41:34,200
Here, take these.

820
00:41:34,283 --> 00:41:35,785
Why did you turn the light out?

821
00:41:36,577 --> 00:41:37,578
I thought you did.

822
00:41:39,956 --> 00:41:41,874
[ominous music playing]

823
00:41:41,958 --> 00:41:43,042
Tatum.

824
00:41:43,126 --> 00:41:44,293
Stay behind me.

825
00:41:50,800 --> 00:41:51,801
[Mark whispering] Tatum.

826
00:41:54,053 --> 00:41:55,054
Tatum.

827
00:41:57,807 --> 00:41:59,100
[panting]

828
00:42:02,103 --> 00:42:03,312
Dad.

829
00:42:06,649 --> 00:42:08,735
Please, leave her alone.

830
00:42:12,530 --> 00:42:13,990
Mark, put the gun down.

831
00:42:21,414 --> 00:42:23,875
[Mark] Hon, it's gonna be okay.

832
00:42:23,958 --> 00:42:24,876
Just look at me.

833
00:42:29,130 --> 00:42:30,590
[Sidney] It's me that you want.

834
00:42:30,673 --> 00:42:33,009
You just-- you let her go.

835
00:42:38,056 --> 00:42:39,390
- Drop!
- [Tatum screams]

836
00:42:39,474 --> 00:42:40,683
[Mark grunts]

837
00:42:42,268 --> 00:42:43,186
[Mark yells]

838
00:42:43,895 --> 00:42:45,480
[grunting]

839
00:42:55,698 --> 00:42:57,617
[grunting]

840
00:43:02,705 --> 00:43:03,748
- Mark!
- Dad!

841
00:43:03,831 --> 00:43:05,416
[groaning]

842
00:43:10,588 --> 00:43:11,672
Run!

843
00:43:15,093 --> 00:43:16,552
[panting] This way!

844
00:43:19,222 --> 00:43:21,099
[Tatum] What-What are you doing?

845
00:43:23,392 --> 00:43:24,644
Fuck off!

846
00:43:28,564 --> 00:43:30,691
- Where are we?
- We're safe in here.

847
00:43:37,907 --> 00:43:39,909
- You sure he can't get inside?
- Yeah.

848
00:43:39,992 --> 00:43:41,410
- What is that?
- It's another way out.

849
00:43:41,494 --> 00:43:43,037
I need to get your dad. You stay here.

850
00:43:43,121 --> 00:43:44,413
No, you can't leave me, Mom!

851
00:43:45,623 --> 00:43:46,666
- [thud]
- [screams]

852
00:43:46,749 --> 00:43:48,167
Let me go with you, please!

853
00:43:48,251 --> 00:43:49,752
Okay, hurry.

854
00:43:57,051 --> 00:43:58,052
[Tatum groans]

855
00:44:01,514 --> 00:44:02,849
[whispering] Down to the end. Go.

856
00:44:02,932 --> 00:44:03,933
Okay.

857
00:44:05,351 --> 00:44:07,019
[floorboards creak]

858
00:44:09,397 --> 00:44:10,857
[tapping]

859
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:13,943
[whispers] Shh.

860
00:44:19,949 --> 00:44:20,992
[tapping]

861
00:44:30,001 --> 00:44:31,252
[tapping]

862
00:44:33,796 --> 00:44:34,630
[gasps]

863
00:44:35,131 --> 00:44:36,507
[screams]

864
00:44:36,591 --> 00:44:38,301
- Mom!
- This way!

865
00:44:39,844 --> 00:44:40,928
[both gasp, scream]

866
00:44:41,012 --> 00:44:42,346
- Mom!
- Go, go, go!

867
00:44:44,140 --> 00:44:45,558
[exclaiming, panting]

868
00:44:48,978 --> 00:44:50,021
[screaming]

869
00:44:53,232 --> 00:44:54,233
Okay.

870
00:44:56,277 --> 00:44:58,571
[both panting]

871
00:45:02,742 --> 00:45:04,160
Shh-- [gasps]

872
00:45:04,243 --> 00:45:05,453
[screams]

873
00:45:11,167 --> 00:45:12,001
Go, go, go!

874
00:45:20,635 --> 00:45:22,011
- [screams]
- Mom!

875
00:45:23,137 --> 00:45:24,138
Go!

876
00:45:43,991 --> 00:45:45,785
[panting] Okay. This way.

877
00:45:52,792 --> 00:45:54,418
[Mark yells]

878
00:45:54,961 --> 00:45:56,545
[grunting]

879
00:46:08,099 --> 00:46:09,517
- Get the police! Go!
- Mom!

880
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:11,978
Help! Somebody help us!

881
00:46:12,478 --> 00:46:14,230
[grunting]

882
00:46:36,210 --> 00:46:38,170
- Hey, are you okay?
- [panting]

883
00:46:38,254 --> 00:46:40,423
- Are you okay?
- Yeah.

884
00:46:40,506 --> 00:46:42,425
- God, I love you.
- I love you.

885
00:46:42,675 --> 00:46:44,552
[dramatic music playing]

886
00:46:47,680 --> 00:46:48,889
Did I get him?

887
00:46:49,390 --> 00:46:50,391
You got him!

888
00:46:50,474 --> 00:46:52,101
Chad, get the camera now.

889
00:46:52,184 --> 00:46:53,602
Mindy, set up for a remote.

890
00:46:53,686 --> 00:46:55,313
Ma'am, you need to stay
inside your vehicle.

891
00:46:55,396 --> 00:46:57,023
You need to get out of my face.

892
00:46:57,606 --> 00:46:59,108
Mom! Dad!

893
00:47:01,986 --> 00:47:03,654
- Are you okay?
- I'm okay.

894
00:47:03,738 --> 00:47:05,990
- Oh, that was horrifying.
- That was awesome.

895
00:47:06,073 --> 00:47:07,950
Grab the camera.
We need B-roll of everything.

896
00:47:08,034 --> 00:47:09,827
You have to be ready at all times.

897
00:47:09,910 --> 00:47:13,873
In my defense, I wasn't exactly expecting
to be part of vehicular manslaughter

898
00:47:13,956 --> 00:47:15,416
the second we roll into town,

899
00:47:15,499 --> 00:47:17,418
but next time...
next time I will be prepared.

900
00:47:17,501 --> 00:47:19,545
[Sidney panting]

901
00:47:20,755 --> 00:47:21,964
Hey.

902
00:47:24,467 --> 00:47:26,886
- Chief, you gonna be okay?
- Put pressure on it.

903
00:47:26,969 --> 00:47:28,596
Just sit still for a minute.

904
00:47:31,724 --> 00:47:33,351
You're bleeding.

905
00:47:33,434 --> 00:47:34,810
Your point?

906
00:47:34,894 --> 00:47:37,104
[emotional music playing]

907
00:47:41,942 --> 00:47:42,943
How's Mark?

908
00:47:43,027 --> 00:47:45,154
It takes a lot to bring him down.

909
00:47:47,198 --> 00:47:48,991
[sighs]

910
00:47:49,075 --> 00:47:50,826
Gale, he said he was Stu.

911
00:47:51,911 --> 00:47:53,245
I'm sorry. What did you say?

912
00:47:53,746 --> 00:47:54,747
Stu.

913
00:47:57,875 --> 00:47:59,126
Stu Macher?

914
00:47:59,210 --> 00:48:01,087
Dead Stu Macher?

915
00:48:03,047 --> 00:48:04,632
Let's unmask this fucker.

916
00:48:04,715 --> 00:48:07,468
[ominous music playing]

917
00:48:07,551 --> 00:48:08,886
- Chief?
- Do it.

918
00:48:13,682 --> 00:48:15,184
Who is that?

919
00:48:15,267 --> 00:48:18,854
I don't know, but I saw him
today in the coffee shop.

920
00:48:18,938 --> 00:48:20,648
- Are you sure?
- Yeah.

921
00:48:20,731 --> 00:48:23,651
[Mindy] Nobody knows the guy?
Okay, that's weird.

922
00:48:23,734 --> 00:48:26,570
That is weird. It's always
someone you know.

923
00:48:26,654 --> 00:48:28,656
[sirens blaring]

924
00:48:28,739 --> 00:48:30,366
[mysterious music playing]

925
00:48:30,449 --> 00:48:31,826
[indistinct police chatter]

926
00:48:31,909 --> 00:48:34,328
[Chad] You want more B-roll?
We could make a whole movie.

927
00:48:34,412 --> 00:48:35,871
[Gale] I don't know what to say.

928
00:48:35,955 --> 00:48:38,582
I meant to brake and I hit the gas.

929
00:48:45,214 --> 00:48:46,757
Karl Allen Gibbs.

930
00:48:46,841 --> 00:48:49,552
He escaped from Fallbrook
Psychiatric Hospital two weeks ago.

931
00:48:49,635 --> 00:48:50,678
Triple murderer.

932
00:48:51,387 --> 00:48:54,181
Any idea why he'd come after
you or your family?

933
00:48:54,265 --> 00:48:56,267
- No.
- Thanks, Cooke.

934
00:48:57,059 --> 00:48:58,144
Chief.

935
00:48:59,228 --> 00:49:00,229
[sighs]

936
00:49:04,859 --> 00:49:06,193
Well...

937
00:49:06,277 --> 00:49:07,736
He's not gonna hurt anyone else.

938
00:49:07,820 --> 00:49:09,321
No.

939
00:49:10,656 --> 00:49:11,907
This was too easy.

940
00:49:13,534 --> 00:49:14,660
There's always more than one.

941
00:49:14,743 --> 00:49:15,744
Sidney,

942
00:49:15,828 --> 00:49:17,496
Stu Macher is dead.

943
00:49:18,372 --> 00:49:20,291
[sighs]

944
00:49:20,374 --> 00:49:21,959
Watch Tatum for a minute.

945
00:49:24,879 --> 00:49:27,256
[reporter 1] Sidney. Sidney!

946
00:49:27,339 --> 00:49:29,800
One question for you, Sidney!

947
00:49:29,884 --> 00:49:31,051
Can we have a word?

948
00:49:32,219 --> 00:49:35,347
Sidney! What's going on? Over here!

949
00:49:36,599 --> 00:49:37,933
[reporter 2] Can you tell us anything?

950
00:49:38,017 --> 00:49:40,394
What's happening, Sidney? What's going on?

951
00:49:40,478 --> 00:49:41,479
Sidney!

952
00:49:46,942 --> 00:49:49,612
The network texted.
They want us to go live.

953
00:49:49,695 --> 00:49:52,573
- I'll go get Gale.
- No! Don't.

954
00:49:52,656 --> 00:49:54,325
- No. No, I'm not doing this.
- Yes.

955
00:49:54,408 --> 00:49:56,452
They didn't specify it had to be Gale.

956
00:49:56,535 --> 00:49:59,371
- You'll get us fired!
- Do it! Come on!

957
00:49:59,455 --> 00:50:01,207
- Fine.
- [clears throat]

958
00:50:02,374 --> 00:50:05,503
Three, two, one-- Oh, boy.

959
00:50:07,338 --> 00:50:09,965
You try that again,
and I'll rip both your throats out.

960
00:50:10,049 --> 00:50:11,050
- Got it?
- Copy that.

961
00:50:11,133 --> 00:50:14,178
We just learned that Gale Weathers
from the now defunct talk show

962
00:50:14,261 --> 00:50:16,514
<i>Good Morning with Gale Weathers</i>
is in town.

963
00:50:16,597 --> 00:50:17,890
Excuse me, Miss Weathers.

964
00:50:17,973 --> 00:50:19,892
Robbie Rivers, WFPO. May I ask--

965
00:50:19,975 --> 00:50:22,186
- Fuck the fuck off.
- Okay.

966
00:50:22,269 --> 00:50:24,730
You two are a familiar sight.
What are you doing in town?

967
00:50:25,773 --> 00:50:26,774
Just passing through.

968
00:50:26,857 --> 00:50:28,400
With Gale Weathers?

969
00:50:28,484 --> 00:50:31,487
And you just happened
to run over an escaped mental patient

970
00:50:31,570 --> 00:50:33,572
in front of Sidney Evans's home?

971
00:50:33,656 --> 00:50:35,407
What's really going on here?

972
00:50:35,491 --> 00:50:37,076
Why don't you get your own story, Robbie.

973
00:50:37,159 --> 00:50:39,245
Yeah, we're not here to do it for you.

974
00:50:40,454 --> 00:50:43,082
Come on,
give a small-town reporter his big break!

975
00:50:47,086 --> 00:50:49,755
Hey, Sidney.

976
00:50:49,838 --> 00:50:52,508
I'm so sorry this is happening again,
Mrs. Prescott.

977
00:50:53,759 --> 00:50:55,469
Mrs. Evans, Lucas.

978
00:50:55,553 --> 00:50:57,596
Right, yeah. Uh...

979
00:50:57,680 --> 00:50:58,847
Sorry, that's what I meant.

980
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:01,559
Lucas, do you know anything about A.I.?

981
00:51:01,642 --> 00:51:04,061
A.I.? Uh, I refuse.

982
00:51:04,144 --> 00:51:06,855
That is the death of civilization.
[chuckles]

983
00:51:06,939 --> 00:51:08,691
[Jessica] Why are you asking that?

984
00:51:09,692 --> 00:51:10,985
Just be careful, Jess.

985
00:51:11,068 --> 00:51:12,361
Keep your doors locked.

986
00:51:14,446 --> 00:51:16,282
[Jessica sighs] Okay, come on, let's go.

987
00:51:16,991 --> 00:51:17,992
[gasps]

988
00:51:19,618 --> 00:51:20,869
Oh, you're Gale Weathers. Hey.

989
00:51:21,579 --> 00:51:23,080
- And who are you?
- Uh...

990
00:51:23,622 --> 00:51:24,665
I'm Lucas.

991
00:51:25,416 --> 00:51:26,417
What are you doing here?

992
00:51:26,500 --> 00:51:29,128
He's my son, and we live next door.

993
00:51:29,211 --> 00:51:30,713
- We're friends of the family.
- Hmm.

994
00:51:30,796 --> 00:51:31,797
[Lucas] Yeah.

995
00:51:32,631 --> 00:51:34,341
You like horror movies, Lucas?

996
00:51:34,425 --> 00:51:36,385
Yeah, I lo-- I love them.

997
00:51:36,468 --> 00:51:38,178
Especially the <i>Stab</i> movies?

998
00:51:38,262 --> 00:51:39,597
Yeah, I know them inside and out.

999
00:51:39,680 --> 00:51:41,765
- What are you doing?
- Mom, it's Gale Weathers.

1000
00:51:41,849 --> 00:51:43,434
The <i>Stab</i> movies were based on

1001
00:51:43,517 --> 00:51:45,269
her true crime bestseller,
<i>The Woodsboro Murders.</i>

1002
00:51:45,352 --> 00:51:47,980
I know, but I don't like
the way she's looking at you.

1003
00:51:48,063 --> 00:51:51,191
Please leave my son out of
whatever it is you're doing.

1004
00:51:52,484 --> 00:51:53,611
Sorry, kid,

1005
00:51:53,694 --> 00:51:55,237
but you know how this works.

1006
00:51:55,321 --> 00:51:56,322
Yeah.

1007
00:51:56,405 --> 00:51:58,782
Everyone's a suspect.

1008
00:51:58,866 --> 00:52:02,286
Well, yeah, but you killed the killer.
He's dead.

1009
00:52:02,369 --> 00:52:03,370
Hmm.

1010
00:52:04,747 --> 00:52:06,582
How do you know there's just one?

1011
00:52:08,250 --> 00:52:09,251
Excuse me.

1012
00:52:09,335 --> 00:52:11,712
- [scoffs]
- Whoa.

1013
00:52:11,795 --> 00:52:15,257
Until this is over, I want you
to stay away from this house.

1014
00:52:16,091 --> 00:52:17,259
Come on, let's go.

1015
00:52:22,806 --> 00:52:24,725
[Sidney] How did you know to come?

1016
00:52:24,808 --> 00:52:27,478
When the news broke about
the two murders at the Macher house,

1017
00:52:27,561 --> 00:52:31,106
a flock of reporters
raced to get there, but...

1018
00:52:31,190 --> 00:52:33,859
my Sidney-sense told me
that Woodsboro was played out.

1019
00:52:33,942 --> 00:52:37,863
Mark is having the recorded calls
analyzed to confirm they're fake.

1020
00:52:37,946 --> 00:52:39,948
Is it possible they're real?

1021
00:52:40,032 --> 00:52:41,659
Could Stu be alive?

1022
00:52:41,742 --> 00:52:45,746
That would be the better story,
but it's... too far-fetched.

1023
00:52:45,829 --> 00:52:47,247
[Gale] Hmm.

1024
00:52:50,209 --> 00:52:51,543
What's going on?

1025
00:52:52,336 --> 00:52:54,296
Oh, I just have
some nerve damage from the...

1026
00:52:54,380 --> 00:52:56,465
from the attack in New York.

1027
00:52:56,548 --> 00:52:57,800
You're lucky you sat that one out.

1028
00:52:57,883 --> 00:52:59,510
It-it was brutal.

1029
00:53:00,386 --> 00:53:01,470
Thank you.

1030
00:53:01,553 --> 00:53:02,763
It's nice to meet you, Tatum.

1031
00:53:02,846 --> 00:53:04,556
Mmm. Tatum?

1032
00:53:05,683 --> 00:53:07,434
- Tatum as in...
- That Tatum.

1033
00:53:07,518 --> 00:53:08,811
Yeah.

1034
00:53:08,894 --> 00:53:10,145
What do you two do for Gale?

1035
00:53:10,229 --> 00:53:11,647
We're her hot interns.

1036
00:53:11,730 --> 00:53:15,234
Ever since she got axed,
she's been trying to go back to her roots.

1037
00:53:15,317 --> 00:53:18,278
So she's rebranding herself
as a crime reporter.

1038
00:53:18,362 --> 00:53:19,863
She's teaching us
all she knows about the biz.

1039
00:53:19,947 --> 00:53:21,657
- Don't say "biz."
- Yep.

1040
00:53:21,740 --> 00:53:24,827
It's more like we're showing Gale
the ropes of making premium content.

1041
00:53:24,910 --> 00:53:26,161
Don't say "content."

1042
00:53:26,245 --> 00:53:27,454
It's going great.

1043
00:53:27,538 --> 00:53:29,081
Except Mindy keeps trying to
steal Gale's thunder.

1044
00:53:29,164 --> 00:53:31,375
- I'm the face of the future.
- Sure.

1045
00:53:31,458 --> 00:53:34,086
But in the meantime,
we're learning all about fading careers

1046
00:53:34,169 --> 00:53:35,629
and failed comebacks.

1047
00:53:37,631 --> 00:53:38,924
[Gale] Where are we gonna start?

1048
00:53:40,008 --> 00:53:42,511
S-Start what? I'm...

1049
00:53:44,138 --> 00:53:45,472
I'm not starting anything.

1050
00:53:45,556 --> 00:53:48,100
We have to find out who's behind this.

1051
00:53:48,183 --> 00:53:51,270
That guy in the road, Karl Gibbs,
is not some random Killer.

1052
00:53:51,353 --> 00:53:53,897
It's always someone
connected to your past.

1053
00:53:53,981 --> 00:53:55,274
The police can handle it.

1054
00:53:55,357 --> 00:53:58,402
That would be your husband.
And we need to help him.

1055
00:53:59,153 --> 00:54:00,946
Don't you want to know who's behind this?

1056
00:54:01,029 --> 00:54:03,490
Gale, I can't anymore.

1057
00:54:03,574 --> 00:54:06,785
I need to be with my family,
I need to know they're safe.

1058
00:54:06,869 --> 00:54:08,078
That's why you need to help me.

1059
00:54:08,162 --> 00:54:10,581
Whoever is targeting you
is not gonna stop...

1060
00:54:10,664 --> 00:54:12,166
- [phone ringing]
- ...you know that.

1061
00:54:16,628 --> 00:54:20,257
<i>Oh, slap my face,
if it isn't the Gale Weathers!</i>

1062
00:54:20,340 --> 00:54:21,467
<i>Hi. Oh, my God,</i>

1063
00:54:21,550 --> 00:54:23,886
<i>I am so sorry your show got canceled</i>

1064
00:54:23,969 --> 00:54:25,721
<i>and then you got fired.</i>

1065
00:54:25,804 --> 00:54:28,348
I wasn't fired.
My contract wasn't renewed.

1066
00:54:28,432 --> 00:54:30,934
<i>So don't care. Not even a little.</i>

1067
00:54:31,018 --> 00:54:33,896
Ugh. I'm so sorry for
running over your friend.

1068
00:54:33,979 --> 00:54:35,939
Can't do your own dirty work, Stu?

1069
00:54:36,023 --> 00:54:37,441
[mocking blabbering]

1070
00:54:37,524 --> 00:54:38,776
<i>Neither can you.</i>

1071
00:54:38,859 --> 00:54:42,196
<i>You brought in some old,
irrelevant hag for backup.</i>

1072
00:54:42,279 --> 00:54:43,489
<i>It's so sad.</i>

1073
00:54:43,572 --> 00:54:45,115
<i>And what happened to the two of you?</i>

1074
00:54:45,199 --> 00:54:46,909
<i>You both had so much spunk.</i>

1075
00:54:46,992 --> 00:54:49,495
You're gonna die, you A.I. asshole.

1076
00:54:49,578 --> 00:54:51,205
<i>We're going to see how fake I am</i>

1077
00:54:51,288 --> 00:54:53,207
<i>when I stab you in the fucking throat!</i>

1078
00:54:53,290 --> 00:54:54,875
<i>Because I'm coming for you</i>

1079
00:54:54,958 --> 00:54:58,337
<i>and I'm gonna love every second of it.</i>

1080
00:54:58,420 --> 00:54:59,421
[chuckles]

1081
00:55:01,590 --> 00:55:03,217
[sighs]

1082
00:55:03,300 --> 00:55:05,010
That was fucking weird.

1083
00:55:08,138 --> 00:55:09,973
Fallbrook Psychiatric Hospital.

1084
00:55:10,057 --> 00:55:12,100
It's a couple hours away.
We'll start there.

1085
00:55:13,811 --> 00:55:14,812
There she is.

1086
00:55:15,854 --> 00:55:17,898
I knew you were in there somewhere.

1087
00:55:17,981 --> 00:55:21,109
You're right. This isn't
gonna stop unless I stop it.

1088
00:55:28,534 --> 00:55:30,285
I'll be back as soon as I can.

1089
00:55:30,369 --> 00:55:32,371
Mom, I want to go with you.

1090
00:55:32,454 --> 00:55:34,373
No, sweetie, it's not safe.

1091
00:55:34,456 --> 00:55:35,457
So why are you going?

1092
00:55:35,541 --> 00:55:36,583
Because I know what I'm doing.

1093
00:55:36,667 --> 00:55:38,001
Mom, please.

1094
00:55:38,085 --> 00:55:39,294
You don't have the skill set for this.

1095
00:55:39,378 --> 00:55:41,129
Well, then show me.

1096
00:55:41,964 --> 00:55:43,966
I don't want to end up like
the other Tatum.

1097
00:55:45,384 --> 00:55:46,385
What?

1098
00:55:47,427 --> 00:55:51,348
You named me after a girl who
got her head crushed in a garage door.

1099
00:55:51,431 --> 00:55:53,308
- She was my friend.
- And she's dead!

1100
00:55:55,227 --> 00:55:57,020
She was a-a victim, not a fighter.

1101
00:55:57,104 --> 00:55:59,439
I want to be a fighter.

1102
00:55:59,523 --> 00:56:01,275
Honey. Listen--

1103
00:56:01,358 --> 00:56:02,776
Nice to know what you think of me.

1104
00:56:04,361 --> 00:56:05,696
[exhales deeply]

1105
00:56:12,119 --> 00:56:15,205
She just lost a friend, so... she's upset.

1106
00:56:16,456 --> 00:56:18,208
I want you to keep her away from Ben.

1107
00:56:18,292 --> 00:56:20,502
He's not to come over here.

1108
00:56:20,586 --> 00:56:23,547
Someone was hiding in the attic.
It could have been him.

1109
00:56:23,630 --> 00:56:28,051
We are running traces on all her friends'
cell numbers, emails and IP's.

1110
00:56:28,135 --> 00:56:31,346
If Ben or any of her friends
are connected in any way

1111
00:56:31,430 --> 00:56:32,431
we're gonna find it.

1112
00:56:36,018 --> 00:56:39,438
She's right, you know.
Me protecting her from this,

1113
00:56:40,314 --> 00:56:41,773
I made her vulnerable to it.

1114
00:57:04,087 --> 00:57:05,088
Right.

1115
00:57:06,465 --> 00:57:07,466
Okay.

1116
00:57:08,550 --> 00:57:11,136
Okay, Terry. Thanks again.

1117
00:57:13,639 --> 00:57:17,643
Woodsboro coroner says there's
no intake form on Stu Macher's body.

1118
00:57:17,726 --> 00:57:20,228
The woman who was coroner
in '96 died three years ago,

1119
00:57:20,312 --> 00:57:21,438
so there's no one to ask.

1120
00:57:21,521 --> 00:57:24,316
So it's a case of lost paperwork?

1121
00:57:24,399 --> 00:57:25,776
Or stolen paperwork.

1122
00:57:25,859 --> 00:57:27,611
Someone who wants to
make it look like Stu's body

1123
00:57:27,694 --> 00:57:29,071
never made it to the morgue.

1124
00:57:30,405 --> 00:57:31,406
Or...

1125
00:57:31,490 --> 00:57:32,908
It's actually Stu.

1126
00:57:32,991 --> 00:57:34,660
- Let's find out.
- Yep.

1127
00:57:35,243 --> 00:57:36,870
- Here's your pass.
- Thank you.

1128
00:57:37,621 --> 00:57:38,622
Here you go.

1129
00:57:38,705 --> 00:57:39,706
Thanks.

1130
00:57:40,958 --> 00:57:42,417
How can I help you?

1131
00:57:42,501 --> 00:57:43,794
Hi, I'm Gale Weathers.

1132
00:57:43,877 --> 00:57:46,338
- I'm a reporter for Channel 7 in New York.
- Mm-hmm.

1133
00:57:46,421 --> 00:57:49,174
- We're doing a story on Karl Gibbs.
- figured.

1134
00:57:49,257 --> 00:57:52,469
The state police, they were here all night
going through his stuff.

1135
00:57:53,178 --> 00:57:54,179
Can we see his room?

1136
00:57:54,930 --> 00:57:55,931
Well...

1137
00:57:57,432 --> 00:57:59,726
[groans]

1138
00:57:59,810 --> 00:58:02,104
Yeah, I guess so. Come on,
it's right down this way.

1139
00:58:03,522 --> 00:58:05,482
So what can you tell us about Karl?

1140
00:58:05,565 --> 00:58:07,109
He was a pretty violent guy.

1141
00:58:08,485 --> 00:58:11,363
Killed three women about 20 years ago.

1142
00:58:14,366 --> 00:58:18,078
Can you think of any reason that he would
go after Sidney Prescott and her family?

1143
00:58:19,413 --> 00:58:21,123
[Marco] No, not that I know of.

1144
00:58:22,624 --> 00:58:23,917
I'm glad you're okay, though.

1145
00:58:24,584 --> 00:58:26,044
Thanks.

1146
00:58:29,548 --> 00:58:32,592
Did you ever hear him talk
about the Ghostface killings?

1147
00:58:32,676 --> 00:58:35,387
Or the <i>Stab</i> movies, or anything like that?

1148
00:58:35,470 --> 00:58:36,680
Not that I remember.

1149
00:58:36,763 --> 00:58:37,973
What about, um...

1150
00:58:38,807 --> 00:58:39,808
him?

1151
00:58:39,891 --> 00:58:41,852
Yeah, that's John.

1152
00:58:42,978 --> 00:58:44,229
John?

1153
00:58:44,312 --> 00:58:45,605
Yeah, as in John Doe.

1154
00:58:45,689 --> 00:58:47,566
He didn't know his real name.

1155
00:58:47,649 --> 00:58:51,111
He had amnesia from the blow to the head
that gave him all those scars.

1156
00:58:51,194 --> 00:58:52,654
When did he arrive here?

1157
00:58:52,738 --> 00:58:54,239
Well, it was before my time.

1158
00:58:54,322 --> 00:58:58,660
I've been here 16 years.
So late '90s, maybe?

1159
00:58:59,870 --> 00:59:02,080
His room was right down there.
You want to see it?

1160
00:59:02,164 --> 00:59:03,582
Yes.

1161
00:59:03,665 --> 00:59:05,792
You know, h-he was a drifter.

1162
00:59:05,876 --> 00:59:08,545
Sleeping on the streets
of California or somewhere.

1163
00:59:09,880 --> 00:59:11,965
And then one day he snapped.

1164
00:59:12,841 --> 00:59:15,218
Attacked a high school girl.

1165
00:59:15,302 --> 00:59:19,431
He was declared incompetent
to stand trial and ended up here.

1166
00:59:20,307 --> 00:59:22,642
- And where is he now?
- He was released.

1167
00:59:24,478 --> 00:59:25,854
Two weeks ago.

1168
00:59:26,646 --> 00:59:28,732
Any idea where he went
after he was released?

1169
00:59:29,941 --> 00:59:30,942
No, I'm sorry.

1170
00:59:31,026 --> 00:59:33,820
But for that information
you're gonna need a court order.

1171
00:59:34,446 --> 00:59:38,450
And I assume that John Doe and Karl Gibbs
spent a lot of time together?

1172
00:59:38,533 --> 00:59:40,744
Oh, yeah. No, they were good friends.

1173
00:59:40,827 --> 00:59:41,995
Yeah.

1174
00:59:42,079 --> 00:59:43,288
[Marco] Very close.

1175
00:59:44,206 --> 00:59:45,624
[leaf blower blowing]

1176
00:59:45,707 --> 00:59:46,708
Hmm.

1177
00:59:58,762 --> 00:59:59,763
Hmm.

1178
01:00:02,682 --> 01:00:03,850
[Mindy] Neighbor boy's sus.

1179
01:00:04,559 --> 01:00:06,311
He's out there staring at the house.

1180
01:00:06,394 --> 01:00:07,771
Not subtle at all.

1181
01:00:08,522 --> 01:00:10,482
I've gone back three days.

1182
01:00:10,982 --> 01:00:12,484
If the Killer was hiding in the attic,

1183
01:00:12,567 --> 01:00:14,277
he had to go into the house at some point.

1184
01:00:14,361 --> 01:00:18,657
Could the footage be hacked?
Clearly the killer is tech savvy.

1185
01:00:18,740 --> 01:00:19,825
- [Chad] I don't know.
- [clears throat]

1186
01:00:19,908 --> 01:00:22,160
Uh, did you two find the towels?

1187
01:00:22,244 --> 01:00:23,245
You got everything you need?

1188
01:00:23,328 --> 01:00:25,247
Yeah, the water pressure was...

1189
01:00:25,330 --> 01:00:27,290
top-notch, so, thank you.

1190
01:00:27,374 --> 01:00:28,667
Yeah. Yeah, of course.

1191
01:00:29,709 --> 01:00:31,002
So, um...

1192
01:00:32,087 --> 01:00:33,130
Why are you here?

1193
01:00:34,506 --> 01:00:37,134
I'm sorry, I mean, um... [scoffs]

1194
01:00:38,885 --> 01:00:40,262
After everything you've been through,

1195
01:00:41,221 --> 01:00:42,222
aren't you scared?

1196
01:00:42,305 --> 01:00:45,016
[chuckles] Scared. Necessity.

1197
01:00:45,100 --> 01:00:48,270
My career trajectory
is to succeed and exceed Gale Weathers.

1198
01:00:48,353 --> 01:00:51,606
And as Woodsboro legacy, it is our duty.

1199
01:00:52,566 --> 01:00:55,068
Our uncle Randy was
really good friends with your mom.

1200
01:00:55,610 --> 01:00:57,779
[Mindy] And I want to uncover
the killer this time.

1201
01:00:57,863 --> 01:00:59,197
She has been wrong a lot.

1202
01:00:59,281 --> 01:01:00,532
That is not supportive.

1203
01:01:00,615 --> 01:01:04,161
Un-Uncover a Killer?
How do you uncover a killer?

1204
01:01:04,244 --> 01:01:05,537
Assemble the suspects

1205
01:01:05,620 --> 01:01:08,456
and then Agatha Christie
them until they break.

1206
01:01:08,540 --> 01:01:10,167
So-- How do you know who they are?

1207
01:01:10,250 --> 01:01:13,086
If history is any indication,
it's likely one of your friends.

1208
01:01:13,170 --> 01:01:14,379
Probably your boyfriend.

1209
01:01:14,462 --> 01:01:16,047
[Chad] Boyfriend's too obvious.

1210
01:01:16,131 --> 01:01:17,632
Unless it's by design.

1211
01:01:17,716 --> 01:01:19,843
- It's not my boyfriend.
- [chuckles] That's cute.

1212
01:01:19,926 --> 01:01:22,596
We need to gather all the suspects
together in one room.

1213
01:01:22,679 --> 01:01:26,016
Well, there's a curfew at sundown.
The whole town's closing up.

1214
01:01:28,435 --> 01:01:29,978
Actually, there might be a way.

1215
01:01:30,061 --> 01:01:32,731
I just would have to figure
out how to get around my dad.

1216
01:01:32,814 --> 01:01:34,649
[Chad] Is that possible?

1217
01:01:34,733 --> 01:01:36,276
He is the police chief.

1218
01:01:36,359 --> 01:01:39,571
But if we can find out who's doing this,
then he can go get them.

1219
01:01:39,654 --> 01:01:41,281
If we can help, we should.

1220
01:01:43,658 --> 01:01:44,743
I'm sick of being useless.

1221
01:01:47,412 --> 01:01:48,914
That was Deputy Cooke.

1222
01:01:48,997 --> 01:01:51,625
They're set up to trace his phone
if he calls me again.

1223
01:01:51,708 --> 01:01:53,543
So we just have to wait for him to call?

1224
01:01:53,627 --> 01:01:56,421
Oh, come on, there's got to be
some way to bait him into calling you.

1225
01:01:58,215 --> 01:02:01,551
What if I gave you what you've
been asking me for since 1996?

1226
01:02:02,969 --> 01:02:03,970
An interview.

1227
01:02:06,514 --> 01:02:08,558
Get the fuck out of here.

1228
01:02:08,642 --> 01:02:10,685
Look, I just need an ETA
on that court order.

1229
01:02:10,769 --> 01:02:12,854
[Cooke] <i>You got it, Chief.
I'll take care of it.</i>

1230
01:02:12,938 --> 01:02:15,357
Good. Okay.
Call me the second Sid's phone rings.

1231
01:02:17,150 --> 01:02:18,151
Tatum!

1232
01:02:18,235 --> 01:02:19,402
[clattering]

1233
01:02:26,826 --> 01:02:28,036
[clattering]

1234
01:04:04,299 --> 01:04:05,300
[electrical buzzing]

1235
01:04:17,020 --> 01:04:18,521
[screams]

1236
01:04:23,651 --> 01:04:25,070
[screaming]

1237
01:04:33,161 --> 01:04:34,788
["Red Right Hand" playing]

1238
01:04:34,871 --> 01:04:39,209
♪ <i>...to the edge of town
Go across the tracks</i> ♪

1239
01:04:40,710 --> 01:04:45,256
♪ <i>Where the viaduct looms
Like a bird of doom</i> ♪

1240
01:04:45,340 --> 01:04:46,466
♪ <i>As it shifts...</i> ♪

1241
01:04:46,549 --> 01:04:49,386
[owner] Okay. Get home safe. Bye, guys.

1242
01:04:49,469 --> 01:04:53,640
♪ <i>Where secrets lie
In the border fires</i> ♪

1243
01:04:53,723 --> 01:04:55,642
♪ <i>In the humming wires</i> ♪

1244
01:04:55,725 --> 01:04:58,770
♪ <i>Hey man, you know
You're never coming back</i> ♪

1245
01:04:58,853 --> 01:05:00,939
♪ <i>Past this square
Past the bridge</i> ♪

1246
01:05:01,022 --> 01:05:03,566
♪ <i>Past the mills
Past the stacks</i> ♪

1247
01:05:05,902 --> 01:05:09,989
♪ <i>On a gathering storm
Comes a tall, handsome man</i> ♪

1248
01:05:10,073 --> 01:05:14,744
♪ <i>In a dusty black coat
With a red right hand</i> ♪

1249
01:05:17,122 --> 01:05:18,331
- Hey.
- Hey, Chlo.

1250
01:05:18,415 --> 01:05:19,833
Ben and Lucas are already here.

1251
01:05:19,916 --> 01:05:22,919
All right. Uh, this is Chad and Mindy.

1252
01:05:23,002 --> 01:05:24,796
Hi. I'm Chloe. Come on in.

1253
01:05:26,965 --> 01:05:28,675
[Chad] So your parents own this place.

1254
01:05:28,758 --> 01:05:31,386
[Chloe] Yes, but they don't know
we're here, so we got to lay low.

1255
01:05:32,470 --> 01:05:33,471
How you doing?

1256
01:05:34,639 --> 01:05:36,182
[Chloe] What are we drinking, kids?

1257
01:05:37,434 --> 01:05:38,810
Here is...

1258
01:05:38,893 --> 01:05:41,187
[singsongy] ...the pepperoni
and mushroom pizza.

1259
01:05:41,271 --> 01:05:42,856
- [Tatum] Thanks, Chlo.
- [Chad] Thank you.

1260
01:05:42,939 --> 01:05:44,524
So what is the deal with you two?

1261
01:05:44,607 --> 01:05:47,652
[Tatum] Um, they want to help us
find out who's doing this.

1262
01:05:47,735 --> 01:05:50,572
What, they think it's one of us?

1263
01:05:50,655 --> 01:05:51,948
[Mindy chuckles]

1264
01:05:53,867 --> 01:05:56,077
Yeah. But I don't.

1265
01:05:57,704 --> 01:05:59,664
So this dead dude from thirty years ago,
he is not so dead?

1266
01:05:59,747 --> 01:06:01,458
How could Stu Macher really be alive?

1267
01:06:02,250 --> 01:06:03,960
Where's he been? Under a rock?

1268
01:06:04,043 --> 01:06:06,004
Nobody recognized him for three decades?

1269
01:06:06,087 --> 01:06:08,923
That's a ridiculous retcon
for any franchise.

1270
01:06:09,007 --> 01:06:11,926
See, this time it is all about nostalgia.

1271
01:06:12,010 --> 01:06:14,804
Hey, Min! We talked about the rules thing,
we said we weren't gonna do that anymore.

1272
01:06:14,888 --> 01:06:16,389
- We're better than that. So just...
- Sorry. Okay.

1273
01:06:16,473 --> 01:06:20,351
So whoever it is wants to
bring Sidney out of retirement.

1274
01:06:20,435 --> 01:06:23,438
She's a scream queen. Scream queens
are not allowed to have happy endings.

1275
01:06:23,521 --> 01:06:27,317
There's a reason they keep putting
Jamie Lee in new <i>Halloween</i> movies.

1276
01:06:27,400 --> 01:06:29,277
