The final girl.

1772
01:37:43,733 --> 01:37:45,735
God, you inspire me!

1773
01:37:47,070 --> 01:37:50,698
So I started planning and doing Pilates,

1774
01:37:50,782 --> 01:37:53,701
and then I pulled a Sidney

1775
01:37:53,785 --> 01:37:55,453
and I killed my husband!

1776
01:37:55,536 --> 01:37:57,080
[both chuckling]

1777
01:37:57,163 --> 01:37:59,123
[Jessica] I got away with it, too.

1778
01:38:00,583 --> 01:38:03,836
And I had you to thank for it. [chuckling]

1779
01:38:03,920 --> 01:38:05,546
But then you went away, Sid!

1780
01:38:05,630 --> 01:38:07,590
And you didn't go to New York.

1781
01:38:07,673 --> 01:38:10,009
A Ghostface attack
doesn't count if you're not there.

1782
01:38:10,093 --> 01:38:11,094
You disappeared.

1783
01:38:11,177 --> 01:38:12,553
Why, Sidney?

1784
01:38:12,637 --> 01:38:15,181
I wanted people to see
there was life after trauma.

1785
01:38:15,264 --> 01:38:16,682
But there isn't for you!

1786
01:38:18,101 --> 01:38:20,937
Trauma is your life.

1787
01:38:21,979 --> 01:38:23,147
When you disappeared,

1788
01:38:23,231 --> 01:38:25,358
do you know how much that hurt me?

1789
01:38:25,441 --> 01:38:28,111
I mean, I couldn't fucking handle it!

1790
01:38:28,194 --> 01:38:29,862
I checked myself into a facility.

1791
01:38:29,946 --> 01:38:31,572
Fallbrook. That's where we met.

1792
01:38:31,656 --> 01:38:34,075
Okay, I'm talking,
so don't interrupt me, okay?

1793
01:38:34,158 --> 01:38:36,411
Great. Fuck. Where the fuck was I?

1794
01:38:36,494 --> 01:38:38,246
Shit. Fuck!

1795
01:38:38,329 --> 01:38:40,706
New York. Pilates. You disappeared.

1796
01:38:40,790 --> 01:38:43,126
- Fallbrook.
- Fallbrook. Fallbrook, yes!

1797
01:38:43,209 --> 01:38:45,795
It was the closest psychiatric center
that I could find

1798
01:38:45,878 --> 01:38:48,381
because I had to be near you.

1799
01:38:50,091 --> 01:38:55,096
And that finally brings us to tonight.

1800
01:38:55,179 --> 01:38:57,932
[Sidney] Okay, Jessica, you're right,
I've been selfish.

1801
01:38:58,015 --> 01:39:00,184
I can do better. We can start over.

1802
01:39:00,268 --> 01:39:01,894
I am starting over.

1803
01:39:06,023 --> 01:39:07,191
By killing you.

1804
01:39:08,901 --> 01:39:10,194
No more baggage.

1805
01:39:11,404 --> 01:39:12,989
I am releasing it all.

1806
01:39:14,240 --> 01:39:15,700
What about Lucas? You have a son.

1807
01:39:15,783 --> 01:39:18,202
Oh, no, no. He's gone, Sid.

1808
01:39:18,286 --> 01:39:20,371
I mean, he was too much like his father.

1809
01:39:20,997 --> 01:39:21,998
And now

1810
01:39:23,416 --> 01:39:25,084
I can have a new beginning.

1811
01:39:29,922 --> 01:39:32,216
Do you think that you've been
a good mother to Tatum?

1812
01:39:33,759 --> 01:39:36,679
I mean, you really haven't taught her
anything useful, am I right?

1813
01:39:36,762 --> 01:39:38,222
- [scoffs]
- [Jessica chuckles]

1814
01:39:39,265 --> 01:39:41,601
You've kept the survivor all to yourself.

1815
01:39:41,684 --> 01:39:44,729
But that's okay.
Because I'm gonna teach her!

1816
01:39:48,357 --> 01:39:50,985
She's gonna watch her mother die.

1817
01:39:51,068 --> 01:39:52,695
Just like you did.

1818
01:39:54,197 --> 01:39:55,823
The cycle continues.

1819
01:39:55,907 --> 01:39:56,949
No.

1820
01:39:57,033 --> 01:39:58,868
[Jessica] You see,
it finally dawned on me.

1821
01:40:00,036 --> 01:40:02,121
I don't need you.

1822
01:40:02,205 --> 01:40:03,664
I mean, none of us do.

1823
01:40:03,748 --> 01:40:07,210
Let's face it, you're kind of
past your prime for a final girl.

1824
01:40:07,960 --> 01:40:10,379
I'm creating Sidney 2.0.

1825
01:40:11,589 --> 01:40:13,174
Watch closely, Tatum.

1826
01:40:21,349 --> 01:40:22,391
Okay.

1827
01:40:23,601 --> 01:40:24,727
Okay, honey,

1828
01:40:24,810 --> 01:40:26,479
you're gonna need
to call an ambulance. Okay?

1829
01:40:26,562 --> 01:40:27,563
What?

1830
01:40:27,647 --> 01:40:29,315
Mom! No, wait! Where are you going?

1831
01:40:29,398 --> 01:40:30,399
Stay with your dad.

1832
01:40:30,483 --> 01:40:32,401
No, no, no, no, Mom! God, no!

1833
01:40:47,750 --> 01:40:48,751
[Jessica whispers] Sidney.

1834
01:40:49,835 --> 01:40:52,338
Sidney...

1835
01:40:52,421 --> 01:40:53,589
Please.

1836
01:40:53,673 --> 01:40:55,132
[clattering]

1837
01:40:55,216 --> 01:40:56,801
- [boom box blares]
- ["Look Out For Me" playing]

1838
01:41:10,314 --> 01:41:11,315
[music stops]

1839
01:41:16,404 --> 01:41:17,572
[screams]

1840
01:41:18,781 --> 01:41:19,782
[both grunting]

1841
01:41:38,009 --> 01:41:39,760
Is that all you've got? [screams]

1842
01:41:43,180 --> 01:41:44,390
[screaming]

1843
01:42:08,789 --> 01:42:09,790
Fuck!

1844
01:42:30,061 --> 01:42:31,354
[Sidney panting, coughing]

1845
01:42:31,437 --> 01:42:32,605
Are you okay?

1846
01:42:33,856 --> 01:42:34,982
You got to shoot her in the head.

1847
01:42:35,066 --> 01:42:36,567
- What?
- Shoot her in the--

1848
01:42:37,860 --> 01:42:38,778
Shit!

1849
01:42:38,861 --> 01:42:40,988
Damn it. Okay.

1850
01:42:45,743 --> 01:42:47,078
Come on.

1851
01:42:51,916 --> 01:42:53,250
[screaming]

1852
01:43:11,644 --> 01:43:12,770
You okay?

1853
01:43:16,649 --> 01:43:19,068
I'm Sidney fucking Prescott's daughter.

1854
01:43:27,535 --> 01:43:28,911
Past my prime.

1855
01:43:30,413 --> 01:43:31,372
Fuck you.

1856
01:43:41,549 --> 01:43:45,803
This is Robbie Rivers with an exclusive
on the scene, live report,

1857
01:43:45,886 --> 01:43:47,888
at the home of police chief Mark Evans,

1858
01:43:47,972 --> 01:43:50,474
where a bloody nightmare
has come to an end.

1859
01:43:58,107 --> 01:43:59,233
[pained grunt]

1860
01:44:06,449 --> 01:44:08,033
Network wants a live remote.

1861
01:44:08,117 --> 01:44:10,161
No way. Too much blood loss.

1862
01:44:10,244 --> 01:44:11,746
I can't hold a camera.

1863
01:44:12,496 --> 01:44:13,914
I was hoping you'd do it.

1864
01:44:13,998 --> 01:44:15,750
I do feel better.

1865
01:44:15,833 --> 01:44:17,710
We're gonna need to frame out
the blood, though.

1866
01:44:17,793 --> 01:44:19,128
I'll get the tripod.

1867
01:44:42,401 --> 01:44:43,903
Thanks for ditching me.

1868
01:44:45,488 --> 01:44:47,114
Seriously, what was that about?

1869
01:44:49,241 --> 01:44:52,036
You have always had my back, Gale.

1870
01:44:53,245 --> 01:44:54,497
I should have gone to New York.

1871
01:44:55,414 --> 01:44:56,749
I should have been there for you.

1872
01:44:56,832 --> 01:44:58,000
No, Sid.

1873
01:44:58,083 --> 01:44:59,919
And I was wrong about something.

1874
01:45:00,836 --> 01:45:02,379
I do trust...

1875
01:45:04,840 --> 01:45:06,091
I trust you.

1876
01:45:16,185 --> 01:45:17,520
You want me to drive you to the hospital?

1877
01:45:17,603 --> 01:45:19,522
- I'd love that.
- Okay.

1878
01:45:19,605 --> 01:45:20,606
Just give me a minute.

1879
01:45:38,207 --> 01:45:40,543
This is exactly what
I didn't want for you.

1880
01:45:43,128 --> 01:45:44,797
I don't think it was up to you.

1881
01:45:52,221 --> 01:45:53,848
Tatum was my best friend.

1882
01:45:55,724 --> 01:45:57,434
She was funny,

1883
01:45:58,602 --> 01:45:59,937
and outspoken.

1884
01:46:00,813 --> 01:46:03,774
Said whatever was on her mind.

1885
01:46:03,858 --> 01:46:05,067
No edit whatsoever.

1886
01:46:07,069 --> 01:46:10,239
And she was strong.

1887
01:46:10,781 --> 01:46:12,908
And fierce.

1888
01:46:12,992 --> 01:46:16,328
She wasn't afraid of anything.

1889
01:46:20,165 --> 01:46:22,877
So that's why I named you Tatum.

1890
01:46:23,919 --> 01:46:26,922
Because that was my wish

1891
01:46:27,715 --> 01:46:28,716
for you.

1892
01:46:30,676 --> 01:46:32,136
To be strong...

1893
01:46:34,179 --> 01:46:35,639
and unafraid.

1894
01:46:39,602 --> 01:46:41,020
What else can I tell you?

1895
01:46:43,314 --> 01:46:44,648
That's enough for now.

1896
01:46:46,942 --> 01:46:47,943
Okay.

1897
01:46:52,197 --> 01:46:54,992
- You know I love you.
- I love you more.

1898
01:46:58,120 --> 01:47:00,080
- Let's go see your dad.
- Yeah.

1899
01:47:32,905 --> 01:47:35,324
["Creepin" playing]

1900
01:49:40,365 --> 01:49:42,951
Three, two...

1901
01:49:43,035 --> 01:49:45,621
It all began last Thursday night
in Woodsboro, California,

1902
01:49:45,704 --> 01:49:48,248
at a house made infamous for the stashing.

1903
01:49:48,332 --> 01:49:51,543
Cut. I got caught between
"stabbing" and "slashing".

1904
01:49:51,627 --> 01:49:52,669
Hey, you suck at this.

1905
01:49:52,753 --> 01:49:53,921
Shut up. Go again.

1906
01:49:54,004 --> 01:49:55,839
Copy that. Three, two...

1907
01:49:56,882 --> 01:49:59,259
Hi. I'm Mindy Meeks-Mar-- I don't know.

1908
01:49:59,343 --> 01:50:01,762
[Chad chuckling] You messed up
your own name, dude?

1909
01:50:01,845 --> 01:50:04,807
Stop laughing!

1910
01:50:07,226 --> 01:50:09,937
Okay. Three, two...

1911
01:50:11,146 --> 01:50:13,232
Hi. I'm Mindy Meeks-Martin,

1912
01:50:13,315 --> 01:50:14,775
three-time Ghostface survivor

1913
01:50:14,858 --> 01:50:16,819
and new reporter for CBS 7, New York.

1914
01:50:16,902 --> 01:50:19,863
[Chad] Oh, my God, I wasn't recording
any of that. One second.

1915
01:50:19,947 --> 01:50:20,948
[Mindy] I hate you.

1916
01:50:21,031 --> 01:50:22,783
["Twisting The Knife" playing]

1917
01:53:42,149 --> 01:53:43,150
[music ends]

1918
01:53:51,491 --> 01:53:52,492
English (US) - SDH